        "hook": "If you rent and can't touch the closet, start with the hangers instead.",
        "beat1": "Rented closets come with one rod and no permission to add shelves, so the only variable you control is what hangs on it. Bulky plastic and wooden hangers each claim their own slice of rail, which is why a rod looks full long before the closet actually is. Slim velvet hangers attack the one dimension a lease lets you change: thickness.",
        "turn": "These are slim velvet non-slip hangers built to save space on the rod, sized for suits and everyday clothes, with the velvet surface keeping garments from sliding off. At 4.8 stars across 235,029 reviews, this is one of the most heavily reviewed hanger sets on Amazon \u2014 a rating that holds up at that volume usually means the basics are consistent, not lucky.",
